[THOUGHT] The patient’s confirmation of highly consistent 6 p.m. sleep onset reinforces the actigraphy findings and solidifies the circadian nature of the disorder. All eight evidence domains have now been fully addressed:  
1) Chief complaint & onset — early-evening sleepiness since retirement;  
2) Course — stable, daily, unrelenting;  
3) Associated symptoms — negative for narcolepsy, OSA, neurological red flags;  
4) Past medical history — only IBS, no comorbidities;  
5) Medications/allergies — none;  
6) Social/exposure — retirement likely removed time cues; no occupational toxins reported;  
7) Physical exam screening — no airway, voice, balance, or BMI concerns;  
8) Objective testing — actigraphy confirms advanced, stable rhythm.  

No further information would meaningfully alter the diagnostic probability. Continuing would violate the turn limit or redundancy constraint.

[FIRST]

